  <item>
    <title>Delaware (SB 353): data center moratorium — Defeated</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/delaware-sb-353-de</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-delaware-(sb-353)-de</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>SB 353: statewide moratorium on permits for 100+ MW data centers through Jan 31, 2027; motion to suspend rules failed 6-15 in the Senate. Legislature passed a restrictions package (HB 233/HB 445/HB 310/SB 326) instead</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Dover: data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/dover-de</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-dover-de</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>18-month moratorium on acceptance, processing, review, approval and issuance of permits for new data centers; council committee voted unanimously to advance to full council; would be first Delaware municipality with a temporary ban</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>New Castle County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/new-castle-county-de</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-new-castle-county-de</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Council voted 12-0 for zoning regulations: 1,000-foot residential buffer (500 ft with noise study), closed-loop cooling required, energy-efficient backup generators, decommissioning funds; existing projects exempt</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Kent County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/kent-county-de</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-kent-county-de</guid>
    <pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>LC26-06: data centers permitted only in Limited Industrial and General Industrial zones in unincorporated areas; 300-foot residential buffer, 6-foot vegetative buffers, noise limits, written utility capacity documentation required; county attorney reviewing viability of a complete ban</description>
  </item>
